Maintainer: KubeOS <mail@kubeos.in>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://kubeos.in/

Package: kubeos-base
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, kubeos-branding, kubeos-cli, kubeos-pause-image, kubeos-metrics-server, kubeos-network, kubeos-storage, kubeos-control-plane, kubeos-dashboard, kubeos-kubernetes, kubeos-containerd
Description: KubeOS: the container platform on top of Debian
 Installs a complete KubeOS node and, through its version, answers the question a Debian
 system cannot answer on its own: which KubeOS is this? The individual components carry
 their own upstream versions and can be upgraded one at a time; this package is the thread
 that ties them together, and it is what "apt upgrade" moves when the distribution itself
 moves.
 .
 It also enables the archive: the KubeOS signing key in
 /etc/apt/keyrings/kubeos-archive-keyring.asc and the repository line in
 /etc/apt/sources.list.d/kubeos.list, so a node can update itself without being
 re-installed from a new ISO.
 .
 And it pins Kubernetes: it depends on kubeos-kubernetes, which names the exact release
 (kubelet, kubeadm, kubectl, kubernetes-cni) this KubeOS runs, so installing this one
 package cannot leave a node with an unpinned or vendor-following Kubernetes.
